content:
{
  "asset": "Pump P-107 - AquaDyne HF-300 end-suction centrifugal pump, serial HF3-22950",
  "priority": "P2",
  "stop_equipment_now": false,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Drive-end vibration 5.5 mm/s RMS falls in Zone C (4.5 to 7.1 mm/s RMS), 'Restricted - plan maintenance'. It is below the Zone D boundary of 7.1 mm/s ('Damage likely - stop the pump'), so an immediate stop is not required by the documented limits. The applicable limit is Figure 3 of the HF-300 O&M manual, used for readings on the bearing housings.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C06"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Vibration has risen from 3.0 mm/s last month (Zone B, 'Long-term operation') to 5.5 mm/s (Zone C), crossing one zone in one month. That is an 83% increase.",
      "citations": [
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Drive-end bearing housing temperature is 76 C. This is above the normal limit of 70 C but below the 80 C alarm and the 90 C trip. The applicable limits are in the HF-300 specification table, measured on the housing surface.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C01"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "No leakage was reported, so the seal-leakage symptom does not apply and seal replacement is not indicated.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Only the drive-end vibration was reported. The manual requires vibration on both bearing housings every week, with the highest reading used for classification. The non-drive-end reading is needed to confirm the zone.",
      "citations": [
        "C06"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "Bearing wear (most likely). It is listed as a cause of both high vibration and high bearing temperature, which are the two symptoms seen together at the drive end.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Shaft misalignment. It is also listed as a cause of both high vibration and high bearing temperature.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Over-greasing. It is listed as a cause of high bearing temperature and may account for the elevated drive-end temperature.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Impeller imbalance or damage. It is listed as a cause of high vibration only.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Cavitation. It is listed as a cause of high vibration only; check NPSH.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Take vibration readings on both the drive-end and non-drive-end bearing housings. Classify the highest reading using Figure 3. If any reading is at or above 7.1 mm/s RMS (Zone D), stop the pump.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Record both bearing housing temperatures and compare them with the limits: normal up to 70 C, alarm 80 C, trip 90 C.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C01"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Check the grease quantity in the drive-end bearing for over-greasing.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Check suction conditions and NPSH to rule out cavitation.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Check shaft alignment with a laser alignment tool. Tolerances are parallel offset 0.05 mm and angular 0.05 mm per 100 mm. Correct the alignment if it is out of tolerance.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Inspect the bearings and the impeller. If either bearing shows wear, noise or high temperature, replace both bearings as a pair: drive-end 6312-C3 and non-drive-end 6310-C3 (manual section 5.3).",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10",
        "C05"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If the casing is opened, for example for back pull-out removal to reach the impeller, fit a new casing gasket HF3-120. Tighten fasteners to manual Table 5; the torque values are not in the evidence provided (see open questions). Use lifting equipment for the 68 kg back pull-out assembly.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10",
        "C02",
        "C01"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If the mechanical seal is disturbed and must be replaced, fit cartridge seal HF3-450B, not HF3-450, and torque the gland nut to 30 Nm per SB-2026-014. Replace shaft sleeve HF3-455 if scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth.",
      "citations": [
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "After any work that moves the motor or the bearing housing, repeat the laser alignment to 0.05 mm parallel and 0.05 mm per 100 mm angular.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "After restart, re-measure vibration on both bearing housings and the housing temperatures. Confirm vibration is back in Zone A/B and temperature is at or below 70 C.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C02"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-512",
      "description": "Drive-end bearing 6312-C3 (replace as a pair with the non-drive-end bearing if wear is found)",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-510",
      "description": "Non-drive-end bearing 6310-C3 (replace as a pair with the drive-end bearing)",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-120",
      "description": "Casing gasket - replace whenever the casing is opened",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "Isolate and drain the pump before removing the back pull-out assembly or opening the casing.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The back pull-out assembly weighs 68 kg; lifting equipment is required.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "While the pump stays in service in Zone C, stop it if vibration reaches Zone D (7.1 mm/s RMS or more). Act on the temperature alarm at 80 C; the trip is at 90 C.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The seal flush is Plan 11 from the pump discharge. Never run the pump dry, including during test runs after maintenance.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Laser alignment: 1.5 h, 1 technician.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Bearing replacement (pair), if wear is confirmed: 6.0 h, 2 technicians.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Mechanical seal replacement, only if the seal is disturbed or damaged: 4.0 h, 2 technicians.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "The manual parts list specifies mechanical seal HF3-450 (component type). Service bulletin SB-2026-014 (issued 14 March 2026) supersedes it with cartridge seal HF3-450B for serial HF3-22000 and above. P-107 is serial HF3-22950, which is at or above HF3-22000, so the bulletin applies: use HF3-450B and do not fit HF3-450.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13",
        "C01"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Manual section 5.2 says to tighten fasteners to Table 5 and implies sleeve inspection. The bulletin sets the HF3-450B gland nut torque at 30 Nm (previously 25 Nm), says no sleeve measurement is needed for setting the pre-set cartridge seal, and requires sleeve replacement if scoring exceeds 0.1 mm. For serial HF3-22950 the bulletin values govern the seal gland. Table 5 still applies to other fasteners, since the bulletin only changes the seal.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "Manual Table 5 (fastener torques) is not in the evidence. Torque values for the casing, impeller nut and bearing housing fasteners must be obtained before reassembly.",
    "What is the non-drive-end bearing housing vibration reading? The zone must be classified on the highest reading of the two housings.",
    "The evidence gives no grease type, grease quantity or relubrication interval, so over-greasing cannot be checked against a specification.",
    "Site NPSH available/required data is not provided for the cavitation check.",
    "Does bearing replacement or impeller inspection require removing the back pull-out assembly and opening the casing? The evidence does not state the bearing access procedure.",
    "Given the rapid rise from 3.0 to 5.5 mm/s in one month, should monitoring be increased above weekly until repair? The manual specifies only weekly measurement.",
    "Is there a time limit for running in Zone C? The manual says only 'plan maintenance'; the target completion date is not defined in the evidence.",
    "A bearing replacement procedure beyond 'replace both as a pair' is not provided (e.g. fitting method, clearances)."
  ]
}
